WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:06.200
- [Mark] All right, Gilbert.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.950
Gilbert, where are you from?

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:09.760
- [Gilbert] I'm from Boyle
Heights, East L.A. area.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.730
- [Mark] East L.A. And
tell me about your family,

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:12.563
you had both your parents?

00:00:12.563 --> 00:00:15.440
- [Gilbert] I got my mom and
dad still in the picture.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.670
Although they've never
been really supportive

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:21.123
of my, uh, how can I say it? My life,

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:24.100
the way I live.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:28.900
Due the fact of drugs and gangs,
and sleeping in the street.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:33.730
Um, they're there but it's like
they're not there, you know?

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:34.563
- [Mark] What--

00:00:34.563 --> 00:00:36.880
- Emotionally unsupportive.
They're just there.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:38.800
- [Mark] What age were you
when you joined a gang?

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:41.010
- Uh, I was fifteen years
old when I joined a gang,

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:42.120
my first gang.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:43.800
The reason I joined was

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:45.970
to feel like I belonged to something.

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:48.100
You know, my parents
where never really there,

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:49.790
they always worked.

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:52.950
I would go to school, come
back home, they weren't there.

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:57.350
No love, no affection, no nothing.

00:00:57.350 --> 00:01:00.763
They bought me toys, but,
you know, to this day,

00:01:00.763 --> 00:01:02.330
even my dad told me one time,

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:06.300
you always had what you wanted
while you were growing up,

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.114
all you needed was love.

00:01:08.114 --> 00:01:12.210
My dad was an abusive father,
he used to beat up my mom.

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:14.730
I started seeing him beat up
my mom when I was 5 years old.

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:15.670
In front of me.

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:17.820
She was always bruised up and everything.

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:20.260
To this day, my mom is in denial.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:21.720
You know, she says that,
"Oh, it never happened,

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:22.680
it never happened."

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.160
But I seen it all.

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:26.080
You know, my dad was a crack head.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:28.300
He lost two properties.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.960
You know, while I was growing
up, we owned two houses

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:31.940
and he ended up losing them

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:33.895
because the people that moved in,

00:01:33.895 --> 00:01:36.410
they were paying him with crack.

00:01:36.410 --> 00:01:39.703
So, you know, eventually
he lost those houses.

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:43.530
But, to this day, I love my dad, you know.

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:45.500
He's my hero, he used to be my hero.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:47.170
I looked up to him because

00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:50.320
he was the type of motherfucker
that could go to work,

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:51.500
he'd go to work,

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:54.130
and he always used to carry a gun.

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:56.190
He used to like drinking by himself.

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:58.070
So, when I was growing up, I would see him

00:01:58.070 --> 00:01:59.880
bumping music with the trunk open.

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:00.990
Spanish music.

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:04.730
He had his cowboy hat on, and
he always carried his pistol.

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:06.150
You know, so I would
look outside the window,

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:08.320
and I would like, admire that, you know,

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:11.100
'cause that's like a
tough badass, you know.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:14.680
But, little by little,
I just, it started--

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:18.630
As I got older, it just
started fading away, you know.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:21.090
'Cause now I'm more mature,

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.237
thinking oh well, you
used to beat up my mom.

00:02:23.237 --> 00:02:24.497
You used to beat me up for nothing,

00:02:24.497 --> 00:02:26.330
you used to get cracked out,

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:28.920
and just whoop me for nothing, for free.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:30.980
You know, I would get my
ass whoopings for free.

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:34.320
So, that was the kind of
environment I got brought up in,

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.153
you know?

00:02:35.153 --> 00:02:39.215
I ran away. I ran away when
I was thirteen years old.

00:02:39.215 --> 00:02:40.200
It was my first time I ran away,

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.810
I got introduced into
my gang in junior high,

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:45.190
so I started chilling with the guys.

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:47.090
You know, one thing led to
another, and next thing you know,

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:49.470
I'm part of my hood. You
know, I got love for my hood,

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:51.320
'cause it'll always be there regardless.

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:53.430
You know, I might disappear
for a minute or what not

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:56.630
but if I need somebody
to-- push comes to shove,

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:58.760
if I really need my homies
to go kill somebody,

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:01.330
they're gonna be right
there and go do it with me.

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:02.853
You know, pretty much.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:08.030
I got introduced to Skid Row in 1996,

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:10.180
when it was really Tent City.

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:13.860
I developed a crack habit.
I used to smoke crack.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.400
I used to go to work,

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:18.070
and I used to spend my
whole paycheck on crack.

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:19.200
I used to go get The Terminal,

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:21.632
down the street, for two days,

00:03:21.632 --> 00:03:25.420
and by Sunday morning checkout
time, I was that broke.

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:27.600
And I would go back to work with nothing.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:28.950
Hungry as a motherfucker.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:31.260
No lunch money, no nothing.

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:34.080
So after that, I started
living out here in the streets.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:37.090
I used to stay right here on
Town, between 5th and 6th.

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:38.680
I used to sell dope.

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:41.040
I used to sell crystal meth and heroin.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.660
And for a good minute, I
was doing it real good.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:46.350
I was cashing in over $1000 every day.

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:47.807
But I learned the hard way.

00:03:47.807 --> 00:03:51.460
The first time I sold
crack on the wrong block,

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:52.817
the Blacks approached
me and they were like,

00:03:52.817 --> 00:03:54.150
"Hey, where's my money at?"

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:55.567
And I was like, "What money?"

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:56.760
"You just sold on my block."

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:59.370
He took flight at me, and
I just started fighting

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:02.200
with like four motherfucking
Blacks right there.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:06.010
I could only do so much,
so I started running away.

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:08.360
They chased me, the pistol fell off.

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:11.370
Luckily, the Lord works
in mysterious ways.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:13.410
The police happened to
just hit the corner,

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:15.300
they flashed at everybody running.

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.130
And they said-- they
pulled everybody over,

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:18.760
the Black's head was bleeding.

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:20.970
And they were like, you know,
what the fuck's going on?

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:22.854
I was like man, fuck that
shit, they tried to jump me,

00:04:22.854 --> 00:04:24.730
I don't give a fuck, you know?

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:26.880
Anyways, they made me go this way,

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:29.970
and they still held them guys back.

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:31.570
But, I didn't learn, I didn't go nowhere,

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:34.070
I was still here, you know?

00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:37.140
Like I sad, I was cashing
in over $1000 every day,

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:39.180
you know, and I would take
care of the whole block.

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:42.337
I would feed everybody,
every fucking body,

00:04:42.337 --> 00:04:43.990
you know what I'm saying.

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:46.061
Uh, but down here,

00:04:46.061 --> 00:04:49.660
aint no righteousness,
no loyalty, no nothing.

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:51.550
Because I used to take care
of these motherfuckers,

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:55.010
my own people, I used to
feed them, feed anybody.

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:57.967
They came out with short money,
I would still bless them.

00:04:57.967 --> 00:05:00.310
Hey I need a wake-up, I'll bless them.

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:01.680
You know, I looked out for everybody.

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:03.130
People that got out of
jail, what's up homie,

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:04.560
what's your purpose right here?

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:05.917
You're just standing
around in my block, g.

00:05:05.917 --> 00:05:08.380
"Oh, well, I don't got nothing to do,

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:10.627
I aint got nowhere to
go." Well check this out.

00:05:10.627 --> 00:05:13.610
I'll give 'em a tent, I'll
give 'em an 8 ball of dope,

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:15.650
you know what I'm saying,
and I'd just put them on.

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:19.990
Hey, you owe me this, and
just do what you gotta do.

00:05:19.990 --> 00:05:23.240
And eventually I started
building my own circle,

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:25.700
my own people, my own crowd, et cetera.

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:27.080
You know, I had every fucking thing,

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:31.690
from women, to electronics,
bikes, furniture,

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:34.623
I had my shit hooked up. Really hooked up.

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:38.980
Um, you know, but it
came to the point where

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:39.813
like I said,

00:05:39.813 --> 00:05:41.880
there's no loyalty down
here, no righteousness.

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:45.760
One of my one crew members
ended up dropping a dime on me.

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:47.710
You know, as soon as I went to go re-up,

00:05:47.710 --> 00:05:49.660
I'll be back, hold this shit down,

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:51.760
you already got what you
got, make your money,

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:53.400
I'll be back, let me go re-up.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:55.040
When I go around to go re-up, I came back,

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:57.120
alright, everybody, get the fuck out.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:59.000
Let me go stash my shit.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.510
And when I stash my shit,

00:06:00.510 --> 00:06:01.930
next thing you know you
just hear the engines,

00:06:01.930 --> 00:06:03.440
(makes zooming noise).

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:05.763
The narcs swooping up.

00:06:06.843 --> 00:06:09.039
"Where's the dope at,
where's the dope at?"

00:06:09.039 --> 00:06:10.440
I'm like, I don't know what
you guys talking about.

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:12.570
And then it came out on the radio,

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:15.950
like 10-4 we just confirmed
that he went to go re-up.

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:18.670
You know, re-up is a certain
word that we use out here.

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:19.823
It's a slang, you know?

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:23.210
Yeah, so, one of these motherfuckers

00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:26.150
ended up snitching on me
when I took care of them,

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:28.620
and I would do anything
for these people, you know,

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:29.870
or at least for my crowd.

00:06:29.870 --> 00:06:32.123
Or whoever shows me loyalty, you know.

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:37.959
I've seen females getting raped out here,

00:06:37.959 --> 00:06:39.850
and you can't really do shit about it

00:06:39.850 --> 00:06:41.550
because it doesn't pertain to you.

00:06:43.910 --> 00:06:46.410
I've met people that been on the hit-list,

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:50.020
from the Mexican mafia, you
know what I'm saying, all that.

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:53.030
And I can't say shit because
it doesn't pertain to me,

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:54.270
it's none of my business,

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:57.160
and if I get involved then the
same thing will happen to me.

00:06:57.160 --> 00:06:59.620
I've been and seen tents
where the homeless are

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:01.003
fixing up hot shots,

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:04.130
for the individual that's on that list.

00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:06.704
You know, and I'm just like fuck, fuck.

00:07:06.704 --> 00:07:09.700
I start feeling some type
of way and everything,

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:14.167
but like I said, it's better
you than me, straight up.

00:07:14.167 --> 00:07:16.587
Out here, if you don't know
how to survive, out here,

00:07:16.587 --> 00:07:18.403
this shit will eat you alive.

00:07:20.850 --> 00:07:24.700
So, you know, I've seen that.

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:28.400
And to this day, I don't
really talk about it.

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:31.190
Who can I talk about it with,
you know what I'm saying?

00:07:31.190 --> 00:07:32.970
Fortunately, I came across this,

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:35.283
and here I am now telling you my story.

00:07:36.690 --> 00:07:39.881
For those that wanna, how can I say it,

00:07:39.881 --> 00:07:43.300
grab it or use it for
whatever it benefits you,

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:46.460
for any type of experience
or what not, by all means.

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:49.350
But if not, then hey, suit
yourself, pretty much,

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:51.480
and learn the hard way like I did.

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:52.820
- [Mark] Do you have kids of your own?

00:07:52.820 --> 00:07:53.750
- I have six kids.

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:54.583
- [Mark] Six kids.

00:07:54.583 --> 00:07:57.360
- I have six kids. My
oldest kid is 21 years old.

00:07:57.360 --> 00:07:58.780
To this day he's reaching out for me,

00:07:58.780 --> 00:08:01.120
but I have nothing to offer him,

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:02.440
so I feel,

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:05.950
I feel worthless in that
aspect where I can't

00:08:05.950 --> 00:08:06.783
do nothing for him.

00:08:06.783 --> 00:08:08.520
- [Mark] Were you ever in his life?

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:11.690
- I was in his life for his
first three years, that's it.

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:14.490
But my baby-mama did me
dirty, she traumatized me,

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:17.910
where I see all females the same.

00:08:17.910 --> 00:08:19.770
You know, I can't be nice to them,

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:22.810
I can't, how you say,
wine them and dine them,

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:26.480
because I start doing
that, they'll fuck me over.

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:27.710
And go with the next man,

00:08:27.710 --> 00:08:30.203
or the motherfucker with the biggest sack.

00:08:31.281 --> 00:08:34.750
I got my daughter, her 15
years old, her quinceanera,

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:36.590
is this year.

00:08:36.590 --> 00:08:37.760
I don't know what exact date,

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:39.040
but I haven't been in her life

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:41.630
for like, the past seven years,

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:45.200
due to a fact that I've been
in and out of prison and jail.

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:47.330
I caught my five year term right here,

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:49.713
selling crack to an undercover cop.

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:54.950
This individual looked worst of the worst.

00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:58.440
He had a dirty-ass neck,
fucking foul clothes.

00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:00.400
He had dust-bunnies in his hair.

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:02.250
You never would've expected.

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:05.190
He asked me for a $20
rock, I served it to him,

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:08.610
next thing you know you
see the narcs swooping up.

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:11.210
I ran inside the liquor
store right here on Crocker,

00:09:12.405 --> 00:09:13.750
in front of the post office,

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:15.845
there used to be a
liquor store right there.

00:09:15.845 --> 00:09:18.204
I ran inside right there
and I threw all the rocks.

00:09:18.204 --> 00:09:19.490
All the crack heads that were in there,

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:21.780
it was like a fucking party.
They were like "Oh shit,"

00:09:21.780 --> 00:09:23.220
started grabbing everything, right?

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:24.770
So I'm like, fuck it.

00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:27.930
So anyways, the police went
in there, they dragged me out,

00:09:27.930 --> 00:09:30.464
and I'm like what are
you guys talking about,

00:09:30.464 --> 00:09:31.920
I don't know what the fuck
you guys are talking about.

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:33.930
Next thing you know, you see
that guy, the undercover cop

00:09:33.930 --> 00:09:36.480
with the dust-bunnies
and dirty neck coming.

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:39.910
He got a fucking big-ass
round badge, a square badge.

00:09:39.910 --> 00:09:42.224
I was like fuck.

00:09:42.224 --> 00:09:45.960
Ever since then, I learned
kinda who to sell dope to

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:48.263
who not to sell dope to.

00:09:48.263 --> 00:09:51.500
I had people going up to
my spot with like $200,

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:52.900
trying to buy some heroin.

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:55.402
And I wouldn't serve them for
the same reason, you know?

00:09:55.402 --> 00:09:57.680
- [Gilbert] So, I guess, like I say,

00:09:57.680 --> 00:10:00.793
you gotta learn the hard way,
and I learned the hard way.

00:10:00.793 --> 00:10:04.490
I got into a lot of fights
with the Blacks out here.

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:07.810
I got stabbed three times
out here in the street.

00:10:07.810 --> 00:10:10.720
I got shot at, I shot motherfuckers.

00:10:12.328 --> 00:10:16.520
I kinda earned my respect
and hold my ground out here,

00:10:16.520 --> 00:10:19.420
but it's not really rocket science

00:10:19.420 --> 00:10:21.720
'cause we're outnumbered
by a motherfucker.

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:25.820
It's like 100 Blacks to one
Mexican out here, you know.

00:10:25.820 --> 00:10:30.022
So, if you survive out
here, know what I mean.

00:10:30.022 --> 00:10:32.183
You gotta learn how to survive.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:38.770
Other than that, you
know, I had good jobs.

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:40.500
I used to do demolition,

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:43.330
getting $42 an hour, prevailing wage.

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:45.083
I used to work for UPS.

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:49.420
To this day, I still
have my UPS I.D. badge,

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:53.173
it's just something
mental for me, you know.

00:10:54.941 --> 00:10:58.650
But, I don't know, I guess
drug addiction can really

00:10:58.650 --> 00:11:01.737
get ahold of you if you can't control it.

00:11:01.737 --> 00:11:04.140
And there's been points in my life

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:07.660
where I can't control it because
I leave everything behind.

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:11.633
From my kids to my baby's
mama, to my good working jobs.

